[- Reference: data-bin / Arrow / Parquet. -]
[page id='ref-data-bin'
  [meta
    title='data-bin: Arrow and Parquet'
    layout='reference'
    nav-order='470'
    audience='user,lookup'
    summary='Bridges the CX Table API to Apache Arrow (in-process) and Parquet (on-disk).'
  ]

  [section id='what' title='Purpose'
    [prose data-bin connects the CX Table API to the columnar formats the analytics ecosystem already speaks — Apache Arrow for in-process exchange, Parquet for on-disk storage. The bridges live in libcx_arrow; the CX side stays format-agnostic.]
  ]

  [section id='shape' title='Mapping'
    [prose A CX table converts to an Arrow record batch with one column per CX column, types preserved end-to-end. Decimal stays decimal, dates stay dates, sized integer widths preserved (i32 stays i32, u16 stays u16), no ad-hoc string round-trips. The reverse direction reads Arrow or Parquet and projects into the CX Table form, where the rest of the Table API takes over.]
  ]

  [section id='cli' title='CLI'
    [code lang='shell' src='''cx table dump orders.cx --to=parquet > orders.parquet
cx table load orders.parquet --to=cx
cx table dump orders.cx --to=arrow > orders.arrow''']
  ]

  [section id='python' title='From Python'
    [code lang='python' src='''import cx, pyarrow as pa
batch = cx.table_to_arrow(cx.parse(open('prices.cx').read()))
print(batch.schema)''']
  ]

  [section id='phases' title='Phase Status'
    [prose Phase A (Arrow round-trip) ships at v0.7.0. Phase B (Parquet writer) and Phase C (read-side schema inference) follow in v0.7.x. See spec/v0_7_0_status.md for current phase.]
  ]

